---
import FeaturePageLayout from "../../layouts/FeaturePageLayout.astro";
import DownloadButton from "../../components/button/DownloadButton";
import DownloadMuseHubButton from "../../components/button/DownloadMuseHubButton";
import Shortcut from "../../components/Shortcut.astro";
---

<FeaturePageLayout
  title="Paste Audio – Insert Clipboard Audio at Cursor | Audacity"
  description="Paste clipboard audio at the cursor or over a selection. Assemble tracks, build loops, and move audio between projects. Free for Windows, Mac & Linux."
  canonical="https://www.audacityteam.org/features/paste/"
  heading="Paste Audio in Audacity – Insert Clipboard Audio at the Cursor"
  standfirst="Insert copied or cut audio at a cursor point, or replace a selection range in one command."
  breadcrumb="Paste Audio"
>
  <div
    class="not-prose my-8 rounded-xl border border-text-primary/10 bg-background-medium p-6"
  >
    <h3 class="mb-3 text-18 font-semibold text-text-primary">
      Paste audio in 4 steps:
    </h3>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-text-primary/70">
      <li>
        Copy or cut source audio (<Shortcut keys="Ctrl+C" /> or <Shortcut
          keys="Ctrl+X"
        />)
      </li>
      <li>Place a cursor or select the destination range</li>
      <li>Press <Shortcut keys="Ctrl+V" /> or use Edit &gt; Paste</li>
      <li>Audacity inserts or replaces based on your selection state</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <h2>What Is the Paste Command?</h2>
  <p>
    Paste inserts audio from Audacity's clipboard into your project. At a single
    cursor point it inserts and shifts following audio, while with a selected
    range it replaces that range. It is essential for assembling takes, creating
    loops, and moving clips across tracks.
  </p>

  <h2>How to Paste Audio in Audacity</h2>
  <h3>Step 1: Copy or Cut Audio to the Clipboard</h3>
  <p>
    Use Copy or Cut first so the clipboard has the content you want to insert.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 2: Place the Cursor or Make a Selection</h3>
  <p>
    Click once for insertion behavior, or drag a time range for replacement
    behavior.
  </p>

  <h3>Step 3: Apply Paste (Ctrl+V / Cmd+V)</h3>
  <p>Use keyboard or menu command to paste immediately.</p>

  <h3>Step 4: Review the Result and Fine-Tune</h3>
  <p>Check alignment and transitions, then trim, fade, or nudge as needed.</p>

  <h2>Paste Behavior Explained</h2>
  <h3>Keyboard Shortcut (Ctrl+V / Cmd+V)</h3>
  <p>
    Paste has no dialog. It executes instantly with current clipboard content.
  </p>

  <h3>Cursor Paste vs Selection Paste</h3>
  <p>
    Cursor paste inserts and ripples later material. Selection paste overwrites
    the selected time span.
  </p>

  <h3>Editing Clips Can Move Other Clips</h3>
  <p>
    Track behavior settings determine whether ripple movement is allowed when
    making room for inserted audio.
  </p>

  <h3>Pasting Between Tracks and Projects</h3>
  <p>
    You can paste into other tracks and even other open projects, as long as
    track type/channel rules are respected.
  </p>

  <h3>Mono and Stereo Rules</h3>
  <p>
    Mono can paste into stereo; stereo cannot paste into mono. Track types must
    match (audio to audio, labels to labels).
  </p>

  <h2>Paste vs Cut vs Copy vs Duplicate</h2>
  <div
    class="not-prose my-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-text-primary/15 bg-white"
  >
    <table class="w-full text-16 text-left">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-background-light">
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-text-primary">Command</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-text-primary">Shortcut</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-text-primary"
            >Core Behavior</th
          >
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-text-primary/10 text-text-primary/70">
        <tr
          ><td class="px-4 py-3">Paste</td><td class="px-4 py-3"
            >Ctrl+V / Cmd+V</td
          ><td class="px-4 py-3">Insert or replace from clipboard</td></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="px-4 py-3">Copy</td><td class="px-4 py-3"
            >Ctrl+C / Cmd+C</td
          ><td class="px-4 py-3"
            >Send selection to clipboard, source unchanged</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="px-4 py-3">Cut</td><td class="px-4 py-3"
            >Ctrl+X / Cmd+X</td
          ><td class="px-4 py-3">Send selection to clipboard and remove it</td
          ></tr
        >
        <tr
          ><td class="px-4 py-3">Duplicate</td><td class="px-4 py-3"
            >Ctrl+D / Cmd+D</td
          ><td class="px-4 py-3">Create copy without using clipboard</td></tr
        >
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Common Use Cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Stitching together best takes</li>
    <li>Repositioning phrases or samples</li>
    <li>Building repeating loops from short clips</li>
    <li>Moving content between sessions</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tips for Best Results</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Zoom in before pasting for frame-accurate placement.</li>
    <li>Use fades at paste boundaries to avoid clicks.</li>
    <li>Keep ripple behavior in mind when editing dense timelines.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Can I paste into another project?</strong><br />Yes, if both
    projects are open and track type/channel compatibility is valid.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Why is paste replacing instead of inserting?</strong><br />You
    likely have a range selected; click once to switch to cursor insertion.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does paste overwrite clipboard content?</strong><br />No, it reads
    from clipboard but does not replace it.
  </p>

  <h2>Download Audacity Free</h2>
  <p>
    Download Audacity for free on Windows, macOS, and Linux to edit with full
    clipboard workflows.
  </p>
  <div
    class="not-prose mt-8 flex flex-col w-full md:w-fit gap-4 items-center sm:items-start text-left"
  >
    <DownloadMuseHubButton client:load />
    <noscript><DownloadMuseHubButton client:load /></noscript>
    <DownloadButton client:load />
    <noscript><DownloadButton client:load /></noscript>
  </div>
</FeaturePageLayout>
